            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50269",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "aiohttp: AIOHTTP: CRLF injection in multipart headers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "AIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to 3.14.0, attacker-controlled input included into multipart/payload headers can be used to modify a request to inject additional headers or similar. In the unlikely situation that an application is passing user-controlled strings into MultipartWriter.append(headers=...) or Payload.headers, then an attacker may be able to modify the request to inject headers or change the contents of the request. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.14.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50269",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-50269\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: aiohttp\nFixed Version: 3.14.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-50269](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50269)\nAIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to 3.14.0, attacker-controlled input included into multipart/payload headers can be used to modify a request to inject additional headers or similar. In the unlikely situation that an application is passing user-controlled strings into MultipartWriter.append(headers=...) or Payload.headers, then an attacker may be able to modify the request to inject headers or change the contents of the request. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.14.0.",
