            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41066",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "lxml: python: lxml: Information disclosure via untrusted XML input leading to local file read"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "lxml is a library for processing XML and HTML in the Python language. Prior to 6.1.0, using either of the two parsers in the default configuration (with resolve_entities=True) allows untrusted XML input to read local files. Setting the resolve_entities option explicitly to resolve_entities='internal' or resolve_entities=False disables the local file access. This vulnerability is fixed in 6.1.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41066",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41066\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: lxml\nFixed Version: 6.1.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-41066](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41066)\nlxml is a library for processing XML and HTML in the Python language. Prior to 6.1.0, using either of the two parsers in the default configuration (with resolve_entities=True) allows untrusted XML input to read local files. Setting the resolve_entities option explicitly to resolve_entities='internal' or resolve_entities=False disables the local file access. This vulnerability is fixed in 6.1.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41066**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|lxml|6.1.0|[CVE-2026-41066](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41066)|\n\nlxml is a library for processing XML and HTML in the Python language. Prior to 6.1.0, using either of the two parsers in the default configuration (with resolve_entities=True) allows untrusted XML input to read local files. Setting the resolve_entities option explicitly to resolve_entities='internal' or resolve_entities=False disables the local file access. This vulnerability is fixed in 6.1.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
