            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53540",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-multipart: Python-Multipart: Negative Content-Length in parse_form buffers the entire body in memory"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Python-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.31, parse_form() did not validate the Content-Length header before using it to bound its chunked read of the request body. A negative Content-Length turned the bounded read into a read-until-EOF, so the entire body was loaded into memory in a single read instead of in fixed-size chunks. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.31."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53540",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53540\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: python-multipart\nFixed Version: 0.0.31\nLink: [CVE-2026-53540](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53540)\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.31, parse_form() did not validate the Content-Length header before using it to bound its chunked read of the request body. A negative Content-Length turned the bounded read into a read-until-EOF, so the entire body was loaded into memory in a single read instead of in fixed-size chunks. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.31.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53540**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|python-multipart|0.0.31|[CVE-2026-53540](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53540)|\n\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.31, parse_form() did not validate the Content-Length header before using it to bound its chunked read of the request body. A negative Content-Length turned the bounded read into a read-until-EOF, so the entire body was loaded into memory in a single read instead of in fixed-size chunks. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.31."
              },
              "properties": {
